@# Small end-to-end runtime example for the WG compiler and materializer.

:: taylor.study.peek [event taylor study]
@heading "Taylor's room"
@choices "What do you do?"

Tired of studying, you're unable to resist stealing a glance at Taylor.
{{npc.taylor.dependent|cap}} gaze is fixed on the textbook, lost in thought.

@if story.taylor.hurt >= 1
Taylor notices you looking and frowns.
@elseif npc.taylor.relationship >= 0.5
Taylor catches your eye and smiles.
@else
Taylor remains focused on the textbook.
@endif

@choice study "Study" -> taylor.study.back
  @icon 📚
  @time 1h
@endchoice

@choice mess "Mess with Taylor" -> taylor.study.mess
  @icon 😈
  @#require player.energy >= 10 "You are too tired."
  @warning "This may annoy Taylor."
  @preview relationship -0.02 "-Relationship"
  @effect relationship taylor -0.02
@endchoice

@choice leave "Leave" -> @exit
  @icon 🚪
@endchoice

:: taylor.study.back [event taylor study]
@heading "Taylor's room"

@onenter
  @effect set story.daily.taylorStudyCompany true
@endonenter

You return your attention to the textbook.

@choice continue "Continue studying" -> taylor.study.peek
  @time 1h
@endchoice

@choice leave "Leave" -> @exit
@endchoice

:: taylor.study.mess [event taylor study]
@heading "Taylor's room"

You reach across the desk and interrupt Taylor's careful notes.

@choice apologise "Apologise" -> taylor.study.peek
  @effect relationship taylor 0.02
@endchoice

@choice leave "Leave" -> @exit
@endchoice
